    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-09-24">September 24, 1948</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Gentlemen:</salute></opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs> has
                    received a letter from a minister<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> of
                    which I am sending you a copy of a paragraph concerning <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Tillich&apos;s</rs>
                    <q><rs type="work" ref="#tillich__JAKRCEZL">The Religious Situation</rs></q></p>
                <p>..... As I write, there is yet one more matter which I recall I was to ask you
                    about. The <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5369" type="person">Rev. David
                    Goto</rs>, who teaches Ethics in this University, has translated <rs type="work"
                        ref="#tillich__JAKRCEZL">the Religious Situation</rs> and wants to know if
                    you possess the copyright, and if so, if you would grant him permission to
                    publish his translation. If the right is yours and you are willing to have him
                    publish his translation, would you write to him and saying you are quite willing
                    to have him do so.<note type="ea">Bei dieser Anfrage handelt es sich um die
                        Übersetzung Tillichs Werke ins Japanische. Die religiöse Lage der Gegenwart
                        erschien 1950 in Japan. Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>: <foreign xml:lang="jap"><rs
                                ref="#tillich__WB479NQU" type="work">現代の宗教的状況:
                            現代欧洲文化の宗教性</rs></foreign> (1950). </note><lb/>Sincerely (signed)<lb/><rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__5368" type="person">Richard A.
                    Merritt</rs><lb/>Union T. S. <q>44</q></p>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Tillich</rs> would like to
                    have an exact information on the copyrights. He, of course, would like very much
                    to have the book published in <rs type="place" ref="#tillich_place_id__710"
                        >Japan</rs>.</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4907"
                            type="person">Secretary to Prof. Tillich</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
